# Shell scripts are executed by `sh`, both as git hooks on a developer's
# machine and on Linux runners in CI. A carriage return in one of those is a
# `$'\r': command not found` that appears on somebody else's machine and not on
# the one it was written on, so these files are checked out with LF regardless
# of the platform.
#
# Deliberately narrow. `* text=auto eol=lf` would rewrite every file in the
# working tree on Windows, which is a much larger change than this problem
# needs.
*.sh text eol=lf
.husky/* text eol=lf
